{
  "decline_reason": "",
  "claims": [
    {
      "text": "Under the Manual, non-payment of the correct prescribed fee can mean that an act is not done, a document is treated as not filed, or an application for registration is treated as lapsed, subject to the notification requirements.",
      "quotes": [
        {
          "ref": "TMM/Part4/1/1/3/1",
          "quote": "If the correct fee is not paid as prescribed in the regulations in relation to: doing an act, the act is not to be done, or is taken not to have been done, if the fee has not paid. filing a document, the document is taken not to be filed if the fee has not been paid, filing an application for registration of a trade mark, the application is taken to have lapsed if the fee has not been paid. However, the applicant or his or her agent must be notified in writing within 14 days that the correct fee has not been paid."
        }
      ],
      "authority": "manual"
    },
    {
      "text": "The Manual's Part 2 guidance says that, if notification of an underpayment is not given within 14 working days, the application, notice or request is treated as filed, but the unpaid amount remains a debt to the Commonwealth.",
      "quotes": [
        {
          "ref": "TMM/Part2/4/part-2-4-3-fee-not-paid-or-underpaid",
          "quote": "Where the Registrar fails to notify the person of an underpayment within 14 working days of the person making an application, notice or request, then the application, notice or request is treated as filed despite the failure to pay the relevant fee (reg 21.21A(2)). However, reg 21.21A(2) does not have the effect of waiving the fee. The fee or amount unpaid remains a debt owed to the Commonwealth."
        }
      ],
      "authority": "manual"
    },
    {
      "text": "The Manual says that the Registrar must not perform an act for which a fee is payable, such as examination, until that fee has been paid.",
      "quotes": [
        {
          "ref": "TMM/Part2/4/part-2-4-3-fee-not-paid-or-underpaid",
          "quote": "If a fee is payable in respect of the doing of an act by the Registrar (such as the examination of a trade mark), the Registrar must not do that act until the fee has been paid (reg 21.21A(1))."
        }
      ],
      "authority": "manual"
    },
    {
      "text": "I cannot resolve the difference between the Manual's references to ‘14 days’ and ‘14 working days’ from the supplied legislation, which does not include the relevant notification provisions.",
      "quotes": [],
      "authority": "none"
    },
    {
      "text": "For an incorrect fee notified within 14 days of payment, the Manual says that any fees paid will be refunded after two months if the deficiency is not made good.",
      "quotes": [
        {
          "ref": "TMM/Part4/2/2/5",
          "quote": "If, within 14 days of a fee being paid for the doing of an act or the filing of a document, the Registrar notifies the person who did the act or filed the document that the correct fee was not paid, the act is taken as not done or the document is taken as not filed until the deficiency in the fee is made good. If the deficiency is not made good, any fees paid will be refunded after two months."
        }
      ],
      "authority": "manual"
    },
    {
      "text": "The Manual lists overpayment, documents treated as not filed, duplicate payments, officer error and inapplicable payments as circumstances for refunds.",
      "quotes": [
        {
          "ref": "TMM/Part4/5#1",
          "quote": "Fees are refunded where: The fee has been overpaid; Applications or other documents are taken not to have been filed; A fee is a duplicate payment; A fee has been incurred as a result of an officer error; or An inapplicable payment has been submitted by the customer."
        }
      ],
      "authority": "manual"
    },
    {
      "text": "For liability arising from a trade marks officer's error or omission, the Manual says that the Registrar may remit all or part of an unpaid fee or refund all or part of a paid fee.",
      "quotes": [
        {
          "ref": "TMM/Part4/2/2/1",
          "quote": "If a person becomes liable to pay a fee because of an error or omission on the part of a trade marks officer, the Registrar may remit the whole or part of the fee if the fee has not been paid, or refund the whole or part of the fee to that person if the fee has been paid."
        }
      ],
      "authority": "manual"
    },
    {
      "text": "The supplied extract of regulation 21.24(1) identifies liability caused by an employee's error or omission as its triggering circumstance, but stops before specifying what the Registrar may do.",
      "quotes": [
        {
          "ref": "TMR1995/r21.24(1)",
          "quote": "(1) If, because of an error or omission by an employee, a person becomes liable to pay a fee for which the person would not otherwise have been liable, the Registrar may:"
        }
      ],
      "authority": "legislation"
    },
    {
      "text": "The Manual requires refunds or waivers to be considered and approved by the appropriate delegate, where necessary, before processing.",
      "quotes": [
        {
          "ref": "TMM/Part4/5#1",
          "quote": "All refunds or waivers must be considered and approved by the appropriate delegate, where necessary, before being processed."
        }
      ],
      "authority": "manual"
    },
    {
      "text": "For a non-applicable fee, the Manual directs staff to arrange a refund by emailing MDB_OMW@ipaustralia.gov.au with the trade mark number, the fee to be refunded and the reason.",
      "quotes": [
        {
          "ref": "TMM/Part4/5/5/7",
          "quote": "If a customer has paid a non-applicable fee (e.g., for an extra class that can/will not be added), a refund needs to be arranged. To organise the refund, email MDB_OMW@ipaustralia.gov.au with: the trade mark number. the fee to be refunded. The reason for the refund."
        }
      ],
      "authority": "manual"
    }
  ],
  "declined": false,
  "concepts_used": [
    "GC-0046",
    "GC-0092",
    "GC-0098",
    "GC-0131",
    "GC-0171"
  ]
}
